# Line endings.
#
# This repository mixes CRLF and LF -- ten files are CRLF, the other seventy-odd are
# LF -- and until now nothing recorded which was which. The result was a trap that
# went off repeatedly: editing a CRLF file with anything that writes text in Python's
# default mode silently rewrites every line ending, so a two-line change arrives as a
# whole-file diff. CLAUDE.md once came back 279 lines changed; test_graph_correctness.py
# 655.
#
# `text=auto` puts LF in the index for everything, and the `eol=crlf` lines below check
# those ten files back out as CRLF. So the working tree keeps the endings it has, while
# the index is uniform -- and a tool that flattens one of them to LF in the working tree
# now produces no diff at all, because the index was already LF.
#
# This file alone was not enough. The ten files were committed before it existed, so the
# index still held their CRLF and the spurious diff persisted; `git add --renormalize .`
# in the same commit is what actually closed it. That is why the commit adding this
# carries ten whole-file diffs. They are line endings only -- `git diff
# --ignore-cr-at-eol` on it is empty -- so `git blame -w`, or `--ignore-rev` on that
# commit, reads through it.

* text=auto

# The ten CRLF files, kept as they are.
CLAUDE.md                        text eol=crlf
splitbill/__main__.py            text eol=crlf
splitbill/loader/exr.py          text eol=crlf
splitbill/loader/source.py       text eol=crlf
splitbill/loader/validator.py    text eol=crlf
splitbill/render/text.py         text eol=crlf
tests/test_auto_detect.py        text eol=crlf
tests/test_graph_correctness.py  text eol=crlf
tests/test_validator.py          text eol=crlf

# A real spreadsheet export, CRLF included. Left exactly as it is: the line endings are
# part of what this fixture is testing, and `text=auto` guessing at it would be one more
# thing that can change the end-to-end baseline without anybody asking.
tests/fixtures/bill_realistic.csv  -text

# Binary, so git should never look inside or try to diff them.
*.xlsx  binary
*.png   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
